  "foaf:name": "ICTs4SSF: Building Capacity for Coastal Resilience",
  "sdo:name": "ICTs4SSF: Building Capacity for Coastal Resilience",
  "sdo:description": "ICTs4SSF: Building Capacity for Coastal Resilience empowers small-scale fishing communities to become active contributors to ocean science and climate resilience through co-designed digital tools, training, and inclusive capacity development. Leveraging ABALOBI’s proven ICT platforms, the initiative equips fishers, cooperatives, and youth with skills in real-time environmental monitoring, sustainable fisheries co-management, financial and digital literacy, organisational development,  and digital traceability. In partnership with KU Leuven’s Climares project, fishers serve as a “human sensor network,” reporting local marine changes that inform safety, adaptation, and ecosystem stewardship. This initiative builds long-term, locally embedded ocean knowledge capacity in SIDS, LDCs, and vulnerable coastal states, fostering equitable participation and sustaining benefits well beyond the Ocean Decade.",
